TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"attempt":2,"blocked":true,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/2","kind":"diagnosis","posted":true,"proposal":{"acceptanceCriteria":[{"argv":["bash","-euc","python3 -c \"import json,sys; g=[x for x in json.load(open('silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json'))['campaign']['gates'] if x['id']=='spec-lint'][0]; c=' '.join(g['argv']); assert '--manifest-path /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix/Cargo.toml' in c, c; assert '-p spec-lint' in c, c; assert '--worklist silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json' in c, c; assert '--root .' in c, c; print('ok')\""],"description":"The spec-lint gate in the worklist anchors cargo to the tally.nix manifest and still lints the estate worktree with the same arguments.","id":"spec-lint-gate-manifest-anchored"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","test ! -e Cargo.toml; err=$(nix develop /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix --command cargo run -q --manifest-path /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix/Cargo.toml -p spec-lint -- specs/flashnext --worklist silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json --root . 2>&1 >/dev/null) || true; printf '%s\\n' \"$err\"; ! printf '%s' \"$err\" | grep -q 'could not find .Cargo.toml.'"],"description":"Executing the amended spec-lint gate command from a directory tree that contains no Cargo.toml no longer aborts in cargo manifest discovery and produces no 'could not find Cargo.toml' error.","id":"spec-lint-runs-without-local-cargo-manifest"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","nix develop /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix --command cargo run -q --manifest-path /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix/Cargo.toml -p spec-lint -- specs/flashnext --worklist silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json --root . || [ $? -eq 1 ]"],"description":"The amended gate command, run verbatim from the estate worktree, exits successfully under the gate's own exit-1 tolerance.","id":"spec-lint-gate-green-in-worktree"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","python3 -c \"import json; gs=json.load(open('silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json'))['campaign']['gates']; ids=[g['id'] for g in gs]; assert ids==['repo-tests','spec-lint','flake-eval','fork-verify','receipts-verify'], ids; d={g['id']:g['argv'] for g in gs}; assert d['repo-tests']==['python3','-m','unittest','discover','-s','tests']; assert d['flake-eval']==['nix','flake','check','--no-build']; assert d['fork-verify']==['bash','scripts/verify-fork.sh']; assert d['receipts-verify']==['python3','scripts/receipts-verify.py']; print('ok')\""],"description":"The worklist still parses and the other four gate ids and their argv are untouched.","id":"other-gates-unchanged"}],"dependencies":[],"goal":"Make the spec-lint gate runnable from a task worktree that has no Cargo.toml by anchoring the cargo invocation to the tally.nix manifest, without changing which tree spec-lint lints and without mutating /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix. In silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json, replace the spec-lint gate argv with: bash -euc \"nix develop /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix --command cargo run -q --manifest-path /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix/Cargo.toml -p spec-lint -- specs/flashnext --worklist silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json --root . || [ $? -eq 1 ]\". Leave the preflightArgv, the gate id, and every other gate unchanged. The relative arguments continue to resolve against the gate's working directory (the task worktree), which is the intended lint target; only cargo's manifest discovery is redirected. After the amendment, re-run the container-recipe task's gate set; the committed container/ and results/receipts/ work needs no further change.","kind":"gate-set-fix","paths":["silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json"]},"redacted":false,"retry":null,"taskId":"container-recipe","verdict":"blocked"}
